# tools/ales_zero_cross_witness.rish — the zero-crossing counter: the suite's first analysis rung, reading ALES92's flips as a count (ALES93).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES93.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-225557_fill-ales93-lotus-zero-crossing-counter.md
# Stands on: lotus/schmitt.rye (ALES92 — the hysteresis comparator whose flips this counts, composed over its public schmitt_step and precheck) and
# lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max). The read-only analysis shape is meter's (lotus/meter.rye): a struct that accumulates, accessors that
# report. Every Lotus rung before this one WRITES a clip in place; this one READS a clip and returns a number, changing not one sample.
#
# lotus/zero_cross.rye walks a span and counts how many times the Schmitt trigger flips rail — a zero crossing in the hysteresis sense is exactly a rail flip, so
# the count reads how many times the signal genuinely crossed, past the noise the band already suppresses. The crux is that split-equals-whole rises one level,
# from the samples to a DERIVED count: a flip can land exactly at the seam between two pieces, so the counter carries both the trigger's rail and the previous
# output rail across a call, and a span counted in two pieces equals the whole counted once — the seam flip counted exactly once. The selftest proves it: the
# from-silence convenience equals a fresh counter fed once; it counts exactly ALES92's flips (checked against a by-hand transition count of schmitt's own
# output); a span counted in two pieces with a seam flip equals the whole counted once (the crux); hysteresis suppresses chatter counting (zero crossings across
# a dither a sign comparator chatters on); a known signal counts its known flips; silence and in-band-only count zero; reset re-opens from silence; the source
# clip is byte-for-byte unchanged (read-only); an inverted band refuses BadThreshold and an out-of-range span refuses BadRange with the count and clip untouched.
# Purely local, read-only — the count a pure sample count of rail flips, not a pitch in Hz (no real sample rate yet); no device, no network, no keys, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_zero_cross_witness.rish

say "ales-zero_cross: Language EN — every Lotus rung so far WRITES a clip in place; this one READS a clip and returns a number, the suite's first ANALYSIS move. It counts how many times ALES92's Schmitt trigger flips rail over a span — a zero crossing in the hysteresis sense is a rail flip, so the count reads how many times the signal GENUINELY crossed, past the noise the band already suppresses. It is the oldest activity/pitch estimate there is, the front of voiced/unvoiced detection, of onset and tempo counting."
say "ales-zero_cross: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a crossing is a change between consecutive output rails; the first fed sample sets the rail and counts no crossing, every later sample counts one when its rail differs from the one before. The crux stands out: split-equals-whole rises one level, from the samples to a DERIVED count — a span counted in two pieces, the second carrying the first's rail and previous-rail memory, equals the whole counted ONCE, the seam flip counted exactly once. It composes ALES92's public one-sample comparator, the SAME step the in-place trigger writes, so the counter can never drift from the trigger it counts."
say "ales-zero_cross: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM READ over a span, never written; the band validated through ALES92's own precheck (sample_min ≤ t_low ≤ t_high ≤ sample_max or refuse BadThreshold; a span outside the samples refuses BadRange) before a sample is touched; the count bounded by a named max_crossings, refusing CountFull before overcounting; siloed to lotus/, the count a pure sample count of rail flips (not a pitch in Hz — no real sample rate), no anti-aliasing, no windowing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/zero_cross"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/zero_cross.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-zero_cross: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/zero_cross.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-zero_cross: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-zero_cross: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-zero_cross' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-zero_cross: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-zero_cross line"
